17DEC2024 @hanoihantrakul
Implementation notes:

The griffin lim algorithm requires the forward function wav2mel to be
compatible with the backwards inversion mel2wav.

The previous FrozenUMM-Mel-Decoder used a `torch_wav2spec()` as the forwards
function, which is not compatible with the default griffinlim implementation
in librosa nor pytorch. 

In these configs I use a `GriffinLimHandler()` which ensure the forwards wav2mel
can be correctly inverted back mel2wav using the native pytorch implementation.

Ideally, the mel spectrogram would be inverted back to audio using an ML model,
but at the time of writing I have only implemented GriffinLim. 

Note that the GriffinLim algorithm is also imperfect because when an STFT
is warped into a mel spectrogram, it needs to be warped back to STFT before
GriffinLim can be applied. That warping procedure introduces loss of 
information. 